[size=5][b]⚔ Recommended mods[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60362]The Combat Juice[/url], also by me - a layer of subtle "oomph" all over the combat, visual and audible, without touching any mechanics - every punch feels like it lands.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/59205]Inventory Extender[/url] - shows the Hand to Hand type and the fatigue damage in weapon tooltips.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/54950]QuickLoot[/url] - its loot tooltips show them too.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60361]Combat Sounds Overhaul Overhauled[/url], also by me - katars swing with a fist's whoosh and a blade's under it, knuckledusters with a fist's. Load Combat Sounds Overhaul above [font=Courier New]H2HWeapons.omwscripts[/font].
[/list]

[size=5][b]⚔ How to install[/b][/size]

[b]Requires OpenMW 0.51+[/b]

[list=1]
[*]Install the dependencies: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation[/url] (3.3 or
[/list]

newer) and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60256]Max Yari's Script Services (MSS)[/url].

[list=1]
[*]Install this mod [b]with a mod organiser[/b]: download the archive and drag and drop it into your mod
[/list]

organiser of choice (e.g. [url=https://github.com/ModOrganizer2/modorganizer/releases]Mod Organizer 2[/url] on Windows or [url=https://github.com/grazelandsnomad/nerevarine_organizer/releases/tag/v0.70]Nerevarine Organizer[/url] on Linux). [b]Or[/b]: [url=https://modding-openmw.com/tips/installing-mods/]read this tutorial[/url] on how to install mods using the launcher or completely manually (it's also very easy). The archive has two folders: [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] is the mod and [font=Courier New]01 Glass Glowset Patch[/font] is an optional patch (see Optional below). Mod organisers show an installer that explains them. If you install by hand, add [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] as the data folder, and [font=Courier New]01 Glass Glowset Patch[/font] after it if you want it.

[list=1]
[*]Enable these in the "Content Files" tab of the OpenMW launcher, after ReAnimation:
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Katar.omwaddon[/font] - needs Tribunal and Bloodmoon.
[*][font=Courier New]KatarWorldPlacements.omwaddon[/font] - puts the rare weapons, and a few others, in the world. Needs Tribunal and Bloodmoon.
[*][font=Courier New]KatarTamrielRebuilt.omwaddon[/font] - only with Tamriel Rebuilt, after it: puts the weapons in Tamriel Rebuilt's levelled lists too. Needs Tamriel Data.
[*][font=Courier New]H2HWeapons.omwscripts[/font]
[*][font=Courier New]H2HWeapons_SpellTraders.omwscripts[/font] - optional, it is what lets spell merchants teach Bound Fist.
[/list]
[*]OpenMW Launcher -> Settings -> Visuals -> Animations: "Use Additional Animation Sources" must be
[/list]

enabled.

[list=1]
[*]The weapons are added to the game's levelled lists - the ones merchants' stock, loot and enemies'
[/list]

weapons are rolled from. If you use other mods that edit those lists too, merge your lists once your load order is set, as you would for any such mods:

[list]
[*]Windows: [url=https://github.com/NullCascade/TES3Merge]TES3Merge[/url] or [url=https://gitlab.com/bmwinger/delta-plugin]DeltaPlugin[/url]
[*]Linux: [url=https://gitlab.com/bmwinger/delta-plugin]DeltaPlugin[/url]
[/list]
[list=1]
[*]If you have the launcher's "Factor Strength into Hand-to-Hand Combat" option on (Settings -> Gameplay),
[/list]

set the mod's copy of it to match: Options -> Scripts -> Katars and Knuckledusters. The rest of the mod's settings are there too.

Optional:

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/58693]Unofficial Tamriel Rebuilt Spells[/url] - Bound Fist then grows stronger with your Conjuration, following that mod's bound item settings (turn on its "Scale bound items").
[*][b]PBR[/b]: the weapons come with PBR maps (normal and specular), so metal and crystal catch the light properly under [url=https://github.com/wareya/OpenMW-PBR/tree/0.51]Wareya's PBR shaders[/url] - a small replacement for OpenMW's own lighting shaders. Recommended together with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52114]Aesthetically Shiny Things[/url], which gives the rest of the game the same treatment. OpenMW only picks the maps up with "Auto Use Object Normal Maps" and "Auto Use Object Specular Maps" on (launcher: Settings -> Visuals -> Shaders). None of it is required: without them the weapons look fine with OpenMW's default shaders.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/42762]Glass Glowset[/url]: tick "Glass Glowset Patch" in the installer (or add the [font=Courier New]01 Glass Glowset Patch[/font] folder after [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font]) and the glass katars fit its style - they glow like the rest of the glass set. Needs Glass Glowset installed.
[/list]

Have fun!

[size=5][b]⚔ Mod compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Skeleton and body replacers[/b]: compatible - no skeleton is replaced.
[*][b]Tamriel Rebuilt[/b]: its spell merchants teach Bound Fist too, and with [font=Courier New]KatarTamrielRebuilt.omwaddon[/font] its merchants, chests and NPCs deal the weapons as vanilla's do.
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/58653]Oblivion-Style Spell Casting[/url][/b]: supported.
[*][b]Retextures[/b]: vanilla textures are used as they are, so retexture packs carry over. Glass Glowset also puts its glow in the meshes; the optional patch above gives the glass katars theirs.
[*][b]Other animation mods[/b]: fine, unless they also replace ReAnimation's one-handed attacks while a katar or knuckleduster is in hand.
[/list]

